From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sandeep Gundlupet Raju <sandeep.gundlupet-raju@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] newlib/ssp: Remove write() and raise() calls from
 __stack_chk_fail for bare-metal

newlib 4.6.0 changed __stack_chk_fail to call write(2, ...) and
raise(SIGABRT) before _exit(127).  These syscalls are unavailable in
bare-metal environments (no file descriptors, no signal delivery),
causing the linker to fail when any library compiled with
-fstack-protector is linked against the bare-metal libc.a:

  libc.a(stack_protector.o): in function '__stack_chk_fail':
  stack_protector.c:39: undefined reference to 'write'

For bare-metal targets fall straight through to _exit(127).  The
diagnostic message is dropped because there is no stderr.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [bare-metal specific]
Signed-off-by: Sandeep Gundlupet Raju <sandeep.gundlupet-raju@amd.com>
---
 newlib/libc/ssp/stack_protector.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/newlib/libc/ssp/stack_protector.c b/newlib/libc/ssp/stack_protector.c
index a1b2c3d..e4f5a6b 100644
--- a/newlib/libc/ssp/stack_protector.c
+++ b/newlib/libc/ssp/stack_protector.c
@@ -35,9 +35,6 @@
 __attribute__((__noreturn__))
 __stack_chk_fail (void)
 {
-  char msg[] = "*** stack smashing detected ***: terminated\n";
-  write (2, msg, strlen (msg));
-  raise (SIGABRT);
   _exit (127);
 }
